From 2d9f29dbed41d4b78bda0b7691fdf8ea480872e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Andreyev <257564291+unsound-mint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:50:46 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] mod_optimize: integer exponents instead of real ones

x**2._xp and x**3._xp are real powers; gfortran evaluates many of them
with a call to pow(), which took about a fifth of the run time in a
profile of f_g_cube_fast. x**2 and x**3 compile to multiplications.

Mathematically identical; the results differ only by the rounding of
pow() versus x*x (per-pixel integrated model on a 256 x 256 crop:
median 9e-5, 99th percentile 3.5e-3 relative).

---
 src/mod_optimize.f90 | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mod_optimize.f90 b/src/mod_optimize.f90
index 74ab1a4..b494bcd 100644
--- a/src/mod_optimize.f90
+++ b/src/mod_optimize.f90
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ contains
     
     myfunc_spec = 0._xp
     
-    myfunc_spec = 0.5_xp * sum(residual**2._xp)    
+    myfunc_spec = 0.5_xp * sum(residual**2)    
   end function  myfunc_spec
 
   
@@ -86,15 +86,15 @@ contains
